  "description": "PF12, the fifth arm of the EVALUATE EIBAID at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:124-126, and the only key that is a genuine cancel: it moves 'COADM01C' into CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM and returns WITHOUT performing UPDATE-USER-INFO. The contrast with PF3 in case17 is the point - the two keys look alike from the terminal and do opposite things, and the difference is visible only in what is and is not written.\n\nThe request carries four edited fields; every one is discarded. There is no send at all on this path, no message of any kind, no repository call, and the ten seeded rows are stated unchanged. The empty sends list and the empty expectedWrites list are positive assertions that nothing was produced, not an absence of interest: a judge that ignored an unexpected write here would let a PF12 that silently saved go unnoticed, which is exactly the failure this case exists to prevent. Unlike PF3, PF12 ignores CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM entirely and always goes to the admin menu, even though this invocation arrived from COUSR00C.",
